<h2>Setting Up the LVPIMAN Under Desk Elliptical Machine</h2>
<p>Compact seated ellipticals usually arrive mostly assembled, so setup takes minutes rather than an afternoon. A few steps make the difference between a machine you use daily and one that ends up in a closet.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check the fittings.</strong> Before your first session, make sure the pedals and crank arms are tight. Shipping can loosen them slightly.</li>
<li><strong>Pick the floor spot.</strong> Hard, flat floors with a mat work best. Thick carpet can make the base rock and the pedals feel uneven.</li>
<li><strong>Set the distance.</strong> Sit in your usual chair, place your feet on the pedals and slide the machine until your knees stay slightly bent at full extension.</li>
<li><strong>Test the top of the stride.</strong> Pedal slowly and watch your knees at the highest point. If they touch the desk, move the chair back an inch or lower the seat.</li>
<li><strong>Start light.</strong> Use the lowest setting for the first few days while you get used to pedaling and working at the same time.</li>
</ol>
<p>If you bought a motorized version, place it within reach of an outlet and route the cable away from your chair wheels. Keep the remote on the desk so you never have to bend down mid-call.</p>

