<h2>What Results to Expect</h2>
<p>Light seated pedaling is about 2.0 METs on the Compendium of Physical Activities, compared with about 1.3 for sitting. Moderate effort is closer to 2.8. Using the standard formula (MET × 3.5 × body weight in kg ÷ 200), a 75 kg person at light effort burns roughly 2.6 calories a minute, or a little over 150 an hour.</p>
<p>That is a useful boost when it replaces still sitting, not a substitute for a workout. A realistic routine of three or four 15 to 20 minute blocks a day adds up over a month, and pedaling with genuine effort counts toward the CDC and WHO guideline of 150 minutes of moderate activity a week. Run your own numbers in the <a href="/tools/under-desk-elliptical-calorie-calculator/">calorie calculator</a>.</p>

<h2>Common LVPIMAN Problems and Quick Fixes</h2>
<p>These are the issues owners most often mention with budget seated ellipticals, along with the fixes that usually work.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>It creeps forward.</strong> Add a grippy mat and use a chair that does not roll. This fixes most sliding.</li>
<li><strong>A new squeak appears.</strong> Tighten the pedal and crank fittings and clean around the moving parts. If the noise is inside the housing, contact the seller before the return window closes.</li>
<li><strong>Legs tire quickly.</strong> Lower the setting and slow your cadence. Ten easy minutes several times a day beats one tiring session.</li>
<li><strong>The display numbers look off.</strong> Budget monitors estimate rather than measure. Log your minutes instead and convert them with the <a href="/tools/under-desk-elliptical-steps-calculator/">steps converter</a> if you track steps.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Tips to Make Any Budget Elliptical Last</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Use a mat.</strong> A [[amazon:cubii-mat|non-slip mat]] stops sliding and reduces vibration that loosens fittings.</li>
<li><strong>Check the bolts monthly.</strong> A quick tighten of pedal and crank fittings prevents most squeaks.</li>
<li><strong>Keep it clean.</strong> Dust and pet hair around the crank add friction and noise. Wipe it down weekly.</li>
<li><strong>Do not stand on it.</strong> Seated machines are not built for full body weight, and doing so may void the warranty.</li>
<li><strong>Register the warranty.</strong> Save your order details and the seller's contact in case you need parts.</li>
</ol>

